      retryPrompt: r`Without looking, explain in your own words how a ket becomes a column and an operator becomes a matrix in an orthonormal basis. Then write the two results for $a|1\rangle+b|2\rangle$ and $2|1\rangle\langle1|+3|2\rangle\langle2|$ in the LaTeX box and recall the key words.`,
      sourcePageText: r`B8. Write the matrix representation of the ket |psi> = a|1> + b|2>, in the basis {|1>,|2>}. B9. Find the matrix representation of the operator A = 2|1><1| + 3|2><2|. C3 (first bullet). Explain how a state vector |psi> is represented as a column matrix and an operator A is represented as a square matrix in a discrete orthonormal basis {|phi_n>}.`,
